WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.202
-My first guest tonight
executive-produces and stars in

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:04.403
the new series
"The Flight Attendant,"

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:07.907
which premieres Thanksgiving Day
on HBO Max.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.475
Here is Kaley Cuoco!

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:11.677
Oh, wow!
-Hey, guys.

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:14.747
-It's so good to see you.
-The fans go wild.

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:17.283
-I know. My gosh.
-It's so weird.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.317
Hi, Jimmy!

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:19.852
-Thank you for
coming on the show.

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:21.520
I appreciate this.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:22.956
And I'm psyched about
"The Flight Attendant."

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:24.124
-Thank you.

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:26.993
-Before the pandemic, though,
you were filming

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.260
"The Flight Attendant"
all over the world.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:31.197
-Yes. Yes, it's quite an
international show.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.399
We were in --
Before the pandemic, obviously,

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:36.169
we were in Thailand and then
we were in Rome for a while.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:38.238
So right --
In January of last year.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:39.705
-You were telling me that
in Italy, though,

00:00:39.705 --> 00:00:41.740
you actually felt --
You felt like you were becoming

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.876
more like your character.

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:45.211
-I...
[ Laughs ]

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.279
-You have to tell the story,

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:47.913
'cause it's just, like --
It's awesome.

00:00:47.913 --> 00:00:50.182
-So, my character, Cassie,
is kind of a hot mess --

00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:51.283
a fun hot mess.

00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:53.085
Loves to drink, loves to party.

00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:56.922
So, one night in Rome, me and
the cast decided to go out

00:00:56.922 --> 00:00:58.858
and be like, you know,
one of the locals.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.226
So, we were with a couple guys

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.294
that lived in Rome
and knew the town.

00:01:02.294 --> 00:01:04.764
So they brought us
to this amazing club.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.899
Very small club.
Again, locals.

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:08.668
Like, no tourists.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.736
The place was very small.
You're packed like sardines.

00:01:10.736 --> 00:01:12.405
The music is, like,
loud, bumping.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:15.241
I'm like -- I had never been to
anything like this before.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.776
I walked in, and my first thing
that I clocked

00:01:17.776 --> 00:01:21.414
in this very small club
were open candelabras.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.716
So, like, imagine -- You know,
like "Beauty and the Beast."

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.585
Like, open flames.
-Right. Okay. Yeah. Sure.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:28.254
-Right? So I'm like, "Wow,
that's --" And I clocked it.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:29.822
I'm like, "That's got to be --

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:31.757
That's got to be
a little dangerous."

00:01:31.757 --> 00:01:35.627
So we walk in, and, like,
"Eh, more shots, whatever."

00:01:35.627 --> 00:01:38.131
-Yeah, it's like, "Yeah,
we're too concerned in America.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.800
Come on. Let's be European.
This is cool."

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.001
-"Stop being so worried, Cuoco."

00:01:43.001 --> 00:01:44.503
So, I'm sitting there.
I'm looking at my girlfriend.

00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:47.574
I'm sitting at the bar and I'm
sitting at a tall chair.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:49.842
And there's so many people.

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:51.110
And, all of a sudden,
my girlfriend --

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:54.980
I see her eyes go big,
and I smell smoke.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.850
And I look around and I'm like,
"Do you smell that?"

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:01.687
And she goes -- And I see her,
like, motion that it's me.

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:04.057
Out of nowhere, this man comes
from behind me,

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:06.759
which I still don't know
that my hair

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.093
is the one that's on fire.

00:02:08.093 --> 00:02:09.929
My hair has now caught on fire.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.998
This man comes.
I think he's attacking me.

00:02:12.998 --> 00:02:14.867
And I go, "Oh, my God!
This man..."

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:17.836
And I start hearing,
in the club, people chanting,

00:02:17.836 --> 00:02:20.272
"Fuoco, fuoco, fuoco!"

00:02:20.272 --> 00:02:21.641
And I'm like, "Oh, my God.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.610
Not only is my hair on fire,

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.478
everyone in this club
is recognizing me."

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:27.546
They're, "Cuoco, Cuoco, Cuoco!"
-"Cuoco, Cuoco, Cuoco!"

00:02:27.546 --> 00:02:30.216
Yeah, they're attacking you.
-They're attacking me.

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:31.250
And I'm like, "Oh, my God.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.119
Like, I'm too famous
to be here."

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:34.587
Like, the narcissist
in my brain.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:35.788
I'm like, "You guys,
we have to go."

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:36.990
And they're like,
"But there's fire."

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.157
And they're trying to
put the fire.

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:39.658
And I'm like,
"Guys, please no pictures."

00:02:39.658 --> 00:02:40.693
And I'm hearing, "Fire."

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.195
And I'm like,
"I know I'm on fire.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:44.531
Aah! We got to go.
We got to go."

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:46.365
So, finally,
I realize it's my hair.

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:48.167
I'm thinking they're telling me
I'm on fire.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:50.470
Like, "Hey, baby, you know,
you're on fire."

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.471
And I'm like -- My hair had
completely caught on fire.

00:02:52.471 --> 00:02:53.940
-Uh-huh.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.510
-This man, who I thought was
attacking me in a club in Rome,

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.345
was actually saving my life.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.980
So, when we leave,
me and my friends --

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.015
we're all talking about it.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:03.048
"Can you believe that happened?"

00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:04.284
Like, "I can't believe
I survived that.

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:06.386
Like, my hair.
We're shooting tomorrow."

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:08.254
So, we're with
a couple Italian guys.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.456
They're like, "Yeah, everyone
was yelling 'fire' in the club."

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.458
And I was like, "Well, no, they
were yelling 'Cuoco.'

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:16.161
And he goes, "Well,
they were yelling 'fuoco,'

00:03:16.161 --> 00:03:18.363
which means 'fire' in Italian."

00:03:18.363 --> 00:03:20.266
And I was like, "Wait.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:22.034
They weren't calling
my name in the club?"

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:25.871
-No one cares.
-No one knew who I was.

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:27.440
And I was convinced --

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.942
I'm telling you, one-letter
difference -- fuoco.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:31.444
-And you're like,
"Whoa, they're attacking me.

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.479
No paparazzi, please.
Yes, of course.

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:37.050
We're hot. We're hot.
We're on fire. Yes."

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:40.085
-We laughed for days,
'cause they were like --

00:03:40.085 --> 00:03:42.188
And they walked by -- A couple
of guys that I worked with

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:43.690
that were were like,
"Hey, Fuoco."

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:46.092
Like, it became a joke on set,
and they called me "Fuoco."

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:50.496
And I was like --
It was pretty insane, yeah.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.098
-Well, I'm happy
you survived all of that

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:55.567
and thank that man
who saved you and saved --

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.403
-I was so mad at him.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.405
But now, you know, at least
I can announce that he saved me.

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.440
I really thought
he was attacking me.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.142
But, yeah,
he saved my life and my hair,

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.311
and I owe him a lot.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.312
-Do you want to tell
everyone what

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:08.380
"The Flight Attendant" is about?

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:11.083
-Yes. It's about a boat captain.
I'm kidding.

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:13.052
It's about --
"The Flight Attendant" is about

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:17.623
a stewardess who lives her life
internationally, named Cassie.

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:19.525
She's, kind of like I said
earlier, a hot mess,

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:21.226
loves to drink,
has a lot of issues,

00:04:21.226 --> 00:04:23.162
but she's a blast to be around.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:26.532
And, you know, she goes home
with a passenger,

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.734
very good-looking passenger,
for her one night off

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:30.703
in Bangkok, in Thailand.

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:33.105
And she wakes --
They have a wild night.

00:04:33.105 --> 00:04:36.442
They get completely blackout,
the time of their life,

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.811
and she wakes up
next to his dead body.

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:41.948
And her life is just hell for
the next eight episodes

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:44.383
and trying to figure out who did
this and exonerate herself

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:47.487
and also learn -- It gets
pretty dark as the episodes go

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:50.122
and kind of learning about
herself and her past.

00:04:50.122 --> 00:04:51.156
-I want to show a clip.

00:04:51.156 --> 00:04:53.392
Here is Kaley in
"The Flight Attendant"

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:54.393
on HBO Max.

00:04:54.393 --> 00:04:55.494
Take a look at this.

00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:56.729
-Where are you?

00:04:56.729 --> 00:05:00.766
-Uh, I don't --
This place is so pretty.

00:05:00.766 --> 00:05:03.135
-Yeah. No, okay.
That's not an answer.

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:05.270
Let's see.

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:06.572
Bangkok.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.707
Oh, speaking of getting arrested
in foreign countries,

00:05:08.707 --> 00:05:10.943
do not get arrested there.

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:13.712
The laws are, like, Byzantine.

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:16.348
-Right. Yeah.

00:05:16.348 --> 00:05:17.483
How did you --

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.351
how did you know
that I'm in Bangkok?

00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:21.988
-Oh, when we all took that
girls trip to Tulum,

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:23.588
we turned on our
"find friend" thing

00:05:23.588 --> 00:05:25.124
'cause, like, kidnapping,

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:27.726
and, yeah, you just never turned
yours off, so...

00:05:27.726 --> 00:05:30.229
Listen, you're not, like,

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:32.364
actually in trouble
or something, are you?

00:05:32.364 --> 00:05:35.968
-No, I'm, uh...

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:38.637
hung over in Thailand.

00:05:38.637 --> 00:05:40.306
-More with Kaley
when we come back.

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:42.075
Stick around, everybody.
-Whoo!

